TensorFold
  https://github.com/ashhart/TensorFold
  Copyright (c) 2026 TensorFold contributors. Apache License 2.0 from release 0.6.0 (code written before 0.6.0
  keeps its MIT notice, vendor/TensorFold/LICENSES/MIT.txt).
  Included as the unmodified git submodule vendor/TensorFold (pinned at v0.6.1, 17c73e1). tfvideo calls its
  NVFP4 quantizers and prompt GEMMs (tensorfold.cuda.nvfp4.checkpoint, tensorfold.cuda.nvfp4.linear) and loads
  its CUDA extensions; tfvideo/ext.py wraps tensorfold.cuda.build.load to import extensions prebuilt from the
  same sources. TensorFold's license text is in vendor/TensorFold/LICENSE, its notices in
  vendor/TensorFold/NOTICE and vendor/TensorFold/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.

comfy-kitchen (Comfy Org, Apache-2.0; installed with pip / shipped with ComfyUI, not included)
  https://pypi.org/project/comfy-kitchen/. The engine calls its INT8 attention (comfy_kitchen.sage_attention),
  its fused per-head RMSNorm + split-half RoPE (rms_rope_split_half_) and, for the int8 precision, its INT8
  ConvRot GEMM (torch.ops.comfy_kitchen.int8_linear). tfvideo/source.py reimplements its ConvRot Hadamard
  construction (a 4x4 regular Hadamard raised by Kronecker powers) to read int8_convrot checkpoints.

MiniMax H3 reference implementation (architecture only, no code copied)
  The engine runs inside ComfyUI's own MiniMaxH3Model (https://github.com/comfyanonymous/ComfyUI,
  comfy/ldm/minimax/model.py, GPL-3.0) and replaces only its DiT blocks; tfvideo/minimax_h3.py is an independent
  implementation of a block (RMSNorm + per-token modulation, fused q/k norm + RoPE, attention, SwiGLU, gated
  residuals) checked numerically against ComfyUI's. No source file of ComfyUI is included.

ComfyUI (host, not included)
  The node in comfyui/ runs inside a user's ComfyUI (GPL-3.0) and imports its modules at run time
  (comfy.model_detection, comfy.model_patcher, comfy.model_management, comfy.lora, comfy.sd, folder_paths). bench/
  drives ComfyUI headless to measure the baseline. It is not included.

Quality metrics (downloaded at run time by bench/quality.py, not included)
  lpips (BSD-2-Clause, https://github.com/richzhang/PerceptualSimilarity) and DINOv2 ViT-S/14
  (https://github.com/facebookresearch/dinov2, Apache-2.0) through torch.hub; torchaudio (BSD-2-Clause).

scripts/check-public.sh
